From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 08:25:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: hoist per-batch-invariant state to
 batch->prologue

Apples-to-apples cmdstream comparison vs legacy KGSL (2026-05-28) on the
same Adreno 220 showed freedreno emits ~1.5x more SET_CONSTANT and IM_LOAD
per frame, and ~5x more total state writes accounting for replay. Cause:
fd2_emit_state() writes ALL dirty state -- including FIRST-draw invariants
(shaders, blend, depth, raster, viewport, textures) -- into batch->draw,
which render_tiles() then replays once PER TILE (16x for the heavy 16-bin
scene). KGSL emits per-batch invariant state in a per-batch HEADER that
runs once, with only per-draw deltas in the per-tile loop.

batch->prologue already exists in fd_batch as "preamble cmdstream
(executed once before first tile)" -- used by a5xx/a6xx for blitter setup
and gmem invalidation but not by a2xx at all. Wire it up:

  1. fd2_emit_state(): on the FIRST call per batch (batch->prologue == NULL,
     so all dirty flags fire -> emit everything), redirect the output ring
     to fd_batch_get_prologue(). Subsequent calls in this batch only have
     CHANGED state dirty and route to batch->draw as normal -- those are
     real per-draw transitions that must replay per tile.
  2. fd2_emit_tile_init() (GMEM path): emit batch->prologue after
     fd2_emit_restore(), before prepare_tile_fini_ib and the tile loop.
  3. fd2_emit_sysmem_prep() (sysmem path): emit batch->prologue likewise --
     sysmem batches never go through fd2_emit_tile_init() so they need
     the prologue emitted here too.

Effect: the first draw's state setup (the bulk of fd2_emit_state's output:
SET_CONSTANT pile + IM_LOAD shader uploads + emit_constants) executes
ONCE per batch instead of nbins times. For a 16-bin batch, this cuts the
per-frame CP-executed work proportionally for that hoisted prefix.

Next-session: measure binner_test heavy fps vs legacy KGSL (5.45 fps target,
currently 0.99 fps); if material gap remains, look at the residual per-tile
state in batch->draw (per-draw SET_CONSTANT volume) and the shader
execution side.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++-
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 13 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index 05a69b12a71..7792d5494d9 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -221,7 +221,27 @@ fd2_emit_state(struct fd_context *ctx, const enum fd_dirty_3d_state dirty)
    struct fd2_blend_stateobj *blend = fd2_blend_stateobj(ctx->blend);
    struct fd2_zsa_stateobj *zsa = fd2_zsa_stateobj(ctx->zsa);
    struct fd2_shader_stateobj *fs = ctx->prog.fs;
-   struct fd_ringbuffer *ring = ctx->batch->draw;
+
+   /* HOIST per-batch-invariant state to batch->prologue on the FIRST
+    * fd2_emit_state() call per batch (when ALL flags are dirty -> emit
+    * everything). The prologue runs ONCE per batch from fd2_emit_tile_init
+    * / fd2_emit_sysmem_prep; batch->draw is replayed PER TILE by
+    * render_tiles, so without this hoist the FIRST-draw state (shaders
+    * IM_LOAD, blend, depth, viewport, textures...) re-executes nbins times
+    * per batch (16x on heavy scenes). Subsequent fd2_emit_state() calls in
+    * this batch only have CHANGED state dirty, and go to batch->draw as
+    * normal -- those represent real per-draw state transitions.
+    *
+    * Cmdstream comparison vs legacy KGSL (2026-05-28): freedreno emits
+    * ~1.5x state writes per frame on the same workload, dominated by this
+    * per-tile replay of the first-draw state. KGSL emits invariant state
+    * in a per-batch header. */
+   struct fd_ringbuffer *ring;
+   if (ctx->batch->prologue == NULL) {
+      ring = fd_batch_get_prologue(ctx->batch);
+   } else {
+      ring = ctx->batch->draw;
+   }
 
    /* NOTE: we probably want to eventually refactor this so each state
     * object handles emitting it's own state..  although the mapping of
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
index 7699326c081..65df6bf209a 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -479,6 +479,12 @@ fd2_emit_sysmem_prep(struct fd_batch *batch)
 
    fd2_emit_restore(ctx, ring);
 
+   /* Per-batch prologue (same as the GMEM path): invariant state hoisted by
+    * fd2_emit_state() on the first draw. Must run here too because sysmem
+    * batches never go through fd2_emit_tile_init. */
+   if (batch->prologue)
+      fd2_emit_ib(ring, batch->prologue);
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_RB_SURFACE_INFO));
    OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_RB_SURFACE_INFO_SURFACE_PITCH(pitch));
@@ -620,6 +626,13 @@ fd2_emit_tile_init(struct fd_batch *batch) assert_dt
 
    fd2_emit_restore(ctx, ring);
 
+   /* Per-batch prologue: invariant state hoisted by fd2_emit_state() on the
+    * first draw of the batch (shaders, blend/depth/raster, viewport,
+    * textures). Runs ONCE here in batch->gmem instead of being replayed
+    * inside batch->draw nbins times. See fd2_emit.c:fd2_emit_state(). */
+   if (batch->prologue)
+      fd2_emit_ib(ring, batch->prologue);
+
    prepare_tile_fini_ib(batch);
 
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 4);
